flowchart TB
    accTitle: Running the app — prepare, start, and verify the journey
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. Configure the database and AI credentials, start the default server after its database check, and test the real user journey. Automated tests support this verification but do not replace it. Deployment must also verify the live connection through the actual host. Mock AI avoids provider calls while leaving database work live.
    %% Companion guide: docs/testing-operations.md

    SETUP["Prepare the environment: Database and AI settings"]:::work
    START["Start the default server: Check that the database is ready"]:::work
    RUN["App accepts questions"]:::view
    VERIFY["Check the whole user journey: Ask, follow up, cancel, and export"]:::view
    TESTS["Run automated checks: Requests, SQL, and results"]:::work
    DEPLOY["After deployment: Check the live connection on the real host"]:::work
    MOCK["Optional mock AI: Database queries still run for real"]:::note
    DEBUG["If something fails: Check browser requests and server logs"]:::note

    SETUP -->|1| START
    START -->|2| RUN
    RUN -->|3| VERIFY
    TESTS -->|Supporting checks| VERIFY
    DEPLOY -->|Supporting checks| VERIFY
    MOCK -.->|Optional| START
    VERIFY -.->|If needed| DEBUG

